          "question": "Find the modulus and argument of z = 3 + 4i",
          "type": "complex-analysis",
          "answer": "|z| = 5, arg(z) = arctan(4/3)",
          "workingSteps": [
            "|z| = √(3² + 4²) = √(9 + 16) = √25 = 5",
            "arg(z) = arctan(4/3) (since z is in first quadrant)"
          ],
          "explanation": "Modulus is the distance from origin, argument is the angle with positive x-axis."
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "question": "Express z = 2 + 2i in polar form",
          "type": "polar-form",
          "answer": "z = 2√2(cos(π/4) + i sin(π/4))",
          "workingSteps": [
            "|z| = √(2² + 2²) = √8 = 2√2",
            "arg(z) = arctan(2/2) = arctan(1) = π/4",
            "z = 2√2(cos(π/4) + i sin(π/4))"
          ],
          "explanation": "Polar form is r(cos θ + i sin θ) where r is modulus and θ is argument."
        }
      ]
